@startuml UpsertPermissionBatch

title Upsert Permission Batch API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Upsert Permission Batch Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "m_permission" as m_permission
    database "m_scope" as m_scope
    database "t_permission_scope" as t_permission_scope
    database "t_role_permission" as t_role_permission
    database "t_user_permission" as t_user_permission
    database "t_role_permission_scope" as t_role_permission_scope
end box

user -> page: Submit ordered permissions and optional scope-link changes
activate page
    page -> api: POST v1/author/permission/upsert/batch (JSON, Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**UpsertPermissionBatchCommandHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Lock order: caller user -> all existing target permissions ordered by id -> all ACTIVE referenced scope
                masters ordered by id -> requested owned permission-scope definitions ordered by id -> writes.
                targetPermissionIds is the typed UUID[] of all supplied parent ids (empty allowed). Lock matching
                non-DELETED parents in one query; map rows by id. Check all supplied target ids in original request order
                before permission, any missing/DELETED parent gives 404 E10004 permissions[i]: Permission not found. No
                resurrection. Authorize once from exact PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; do not query live caller
                grants.
                Execution order: whole-input validation (400) -> JWT (401) -> BEGIN -> caller lock/current credentials (401)
                -> all target locks/existence (404) -> one claims permission (403, E10009) -> global
                ACTIVE-master/owned-child locks -> per-permission reference/pre-write conflicts, parent/child writes, final
                count, Q24 deletion guard, Q22 check and indexed mapping -> full result validation -> COMMIT -> one 200.
                Every post-BEGIN failure rolls back the entire batch.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate entire JSON envelope/known unique keys/no query, UTC timestamp and permissions array of 1..100 complete objects before SQL
            note over app, infra
                Generate requestId if omitted. permissions must be an array of 1..100 objects. Each object allows only
                id/name/description/scopes/rowStatus; a supplied id is a non-null UUID. Required name/description are
                non-null nonblank strings, max 64/256 characters, with name matching ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\.[a-z0-9_]+)+$
                without trimming/case-normalization. Parent status defaults to ACTIVE only when omitted, else
                ACTIVE/INACTIVE/DELETED/LOCKED/ARCHIVED; insert-DELETED is 400 E10001.
                Iterate permissions[i] in original input order, not lock order. Validate its child references before any of
                its writes: ACTIVE link requires a returned ACTIVE master (404 E10005); DELETED link skips master ACTIVE
                validation. An existing child must belong to this current parent, be non-DELETED and have the same immutable
                scopeId, else 404 E10004 or 400 E10001 for a changed scopeId. A supplied child cannot belong to a new
                parent. No other parent's data is disclosed.
            end note
            app -> app: Validate required permission code/name/description, optional non-null UUIDs/status defaults and all scope objects; reject parent insert-DELETED, canonical duplicate parent ids and exact non-DELETED names
            app -> app: scopes omitted or [] means no changes; reject null, child insert-DELETED, duplicate parsed child ids per permission and duplicate non-DELETED scopeIds
            alt Invalid whole input or header
                break Reject entire batch
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 (permissions[i] for item validation; no invented index for envelope/count/header)
                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roleIds/name array
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject entire batch
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT; createdBy/updatedBy = caller UUID string
            app -> app: Bind typed UUID[] targetPermissionIds = all supplied parent ids, activeScopeIds = all requested ACTIVE child scopeIds, permissionScopeIds = all supplied child ids; empty arrays allowed
            app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
            note over app, infra
                When any item fails the whole request is rolled back and no permission is changed. `id` must not be
                duplicated in the request, and `name` must not be duplicated among the items that are not DELETED (400,
                E10001). An item without `id` and with `rowStatus` DELETED is rejected with 400 (E10001). The response is
                HTTP 200 for every successful batch, including a batch that deletes. The 403 message has no item position
                (the permission is the caller's, not the item's).
                Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roles before BEGIN. roles is an
                array including [], each object has UUID roleId/non-empty name and roleIds are unique; malformed/missing
                roles is generic 401 E10002, never [] fallback. callerUserId = verified sub, accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact
                JWT, createdBy/updatedBy = caller UUID string; never accept request audit values or flags as authority.
                Begin one READ COMMITTED transaction, lock caller user first, capture fresh server UTC now after that lock
                and recheck JWT exp; require matching hash/caller, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now.
                Missing/revoked/inactive/expired credentials is generic 401 before target reads. Logout/reset share the
                caller lock. Old claims remain usable after grant withdrawal until token expiry; refresh resolves current
                grants.
                Each permission's conflict queries see earlier permission writes in the same transaction. Deleting a
                permission may release its name for a later insert; reversing the order returns duplicate 409 at that
                earlier insert. This is request-order visibility, not a final-state rename plan. Existing parent
                DELETED/ARCHIVED is 409 E10006 while any non-DELETED role/direct-user grant holds it; a DELETED child is 409
                E10006 while any non-DELETED role-scope/direct-user row references it, including inactive/locked/archived
                references. These are business reads, never caller authorization.
                Shared grant/reference writers must lock and recheck target users first, then permissions/definitions in
                ascending id order before creating/reopening bindings. Soft-status invariants are not guaranteed by foreign
                keys; this API's contract and reference SQL fixtures do not certify unmigrated writers. Existing JWT claims
                are not edited by this endpoint.
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Work completes before commit
                note over app, infra
                    Any step may fail after earlier permission/child writes.
                    No item is committed or returned until all items, Q24/Q22 guards and mapping succeed.
                end note
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the caller user
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Lock the caller user
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as user_id
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return locked caller user or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return locked caller user or no row
                alt Caller is missing
                    break Reject entire batch
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now after caller lock; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired while waiting for caller lock
                    break Reject entire batch
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject entire batch
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock existing permissions
                infra -> m_permission: QUERY - Lock existing permissions
                activate m_permission
                    note right of m_permission
                        SELECT
                            p.id as permission_id
                        FROM author.m_permission p
                        WHERE p.id = ANY ('<sequence.targetPermissionIds>'::UUID[])
                        AND p.row_status <> 'DELETED' -- the id of a DELETED permission counts as not found
                        ORDER BY p.id
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED parent ids locked ascending, mapped by id
                deactivate m_permission
                infra -> app: Return non-DELETED parent ids locked ascending, mapped by id
                loop Check every supplied parent id in original input order before permission
                    alt permissions[i].id supplied but missing from locked non-DELETED parent map
                        break Reject entire batch
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 permissions[i]: Permission not found.
                            api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using only exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload live caller grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject entire batch
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to manage permissions.
                        api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check scope
                infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Check scope
                activate m_scope
                    note right of m_scope
                        SELECT
                            s.id as scope_id
                        FROM author.m_scope s
                        WHERE s.id = ANY ('<sequence.activeScopeIds>'::UUID[])
                        AND s.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        ORDER BY s.id
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_scope -> infra: Return ACTIVE referenced masters locked ascending across the entire batch
                deactivate m_scope
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE referenced masters locked ascending across the entire batch
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check existing permission scope
                infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Check existing permission scope
                activate t_permission_scope
                    note right of t_permission_scope
                        SELECT
                            ps.id as permission_scope_id,
                            ps.permission_id,
                            ps.scope_id
                        FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                        WHERE ps.id = ANY ('<sequence.permissionScopeIds>'::UUID[])
                        AND ps.permission_id = ANY ('<sequence.targetPermissionIds>'::UUID[])
                        AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED' -- supplied ids must belong to this permission
                        ORDER BY ps.id
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    t_permission_scope -> infra: Return owned non-DELETED requested child ids with permission_id and immutable scope_id, locked ascending
                deactivate t_permission_scope
                infra -> app: Return owned non-DELETED requested child ids with permission_id and immutable scope_id, locked ascending
                app -> app: Initialize results = []; hold all locks until the one final COMMIT
                loop Process permissions[i] in original request order, not lock order
                    app -> app: permissionId = verified existing parent id or typed SQL NULL for this insert; bind permissions.id/name/description/rowStatus and child values for this item
                    loop Validate every supplied scopes[j] in input order before any writes
                        alt Child rowStatus = ACTIVE
                            alt Requested master absent from ACTIVE master map
                                break Reject entire batch
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 permissions[i]: Scope not found.
                                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                                end break
                            else Check passed
                            end
                        else Child rowStatus = DELETED
                            app -> app: Q23 skip master ACTIVE validation for removing an existing definition
                        end
                        alt Child id supplied
                            alt Child absent from owned non-DELETED definition map
                                break Reject entire batch
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 permissions[i]: Permission scope not found.
                                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                                end break
                            else Check passed
                            end
                            alt Requested scopeId differs from stored immutable scopeId
                                break Reject entire batch
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 permissions[i]: Scope Id cannot be changed.
                                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                                end break
                            else Check passed
                            end
                        else Child id omitted
                            app -> app: New ACTIVE child; request validation already rejected insert-DELETED
                        end
                    end
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Count permission scope definitions
                    infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Count permission scope definitions
                    activate t_permission_scope
                        note right of t_permission_scope
                            SELECT
                                COUNT(ps.id) as definition_count
                            FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                            WHERE ps.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                            AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        end note
                        t_permission_scope -> infra: Return definitionCount including every non-DELETED definition
                    deactivate t_permission_scope
                    infra -> app: Return definitionCount including every non-DELETED definition
                    app -> app: beforeDefinitionCount = definitionCount; require valid nonnegative integer
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Check duplicate name
                    infra -> m_permission: QUERY - Check duplicate name
                    activate m_permission
                        note right of m_permission
                            SELECT
                                p.id as permission_id
                            FROM author.m_permission p
                            WHERE p.name = '<sequence.permissions.name>'
                            AND p.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            AND ('<sequence.permissions.id>' IS NULL OR p.id <> '<sequence.permissions.id>') -- omitted insert id is typed SQL NULL
                        end note
                        m_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED same-name parent excluding optional target or no row
                    deactivate m_permission
                    infra -> app: Return non-DELETED same-name parent excluding optional target or no row
                    alt Another non-DELETED permission holds this name
                        break Reject entire batch
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 permissions[i]: Permission name already exists.
                            api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                    alt Existing parent requested DELETED or ARCHIVED
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check role permission in use
                        infra -> t_role_permission: QUERY - Check role permission in use
                        activate t_role_permission
                            note right of t_role_permission
                                SELECT
                                    rp.id as role_permission_id
                                FROM author.t_role_permission rp
                                WHERE rp.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>' -- destructive parent check or final Q22 guard
                                AND rp.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            end note
                            t_role_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED role grants for this permission
                        deactivate t_role_permission
                        infra -> app: Return non-DELETED role grants for this permission
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check user permission in use
                        infra -> t_user_permission: QUERY - Check user permission in use
                        activate t_user_permission
                            note right of t_user_permission
                                SELECT
                                    up.id as user_permission_id
                                FROM author.t_user_permission up
                                WHERE up.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>' -- destructive parent check or final Q22 guard
                                AND up.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            end note
                            t_user_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED direct-user grants for this permission
                        deactivate t_user_permission
                        infra -> app: Return non-DELETED direct-user grants for this permission
                        alt Either non-DELETED parent grant exists
                            break Reject entire batch
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10006 permissions[i]: Permission is used by roles or users.
                                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                    else Insert or reversible parent status
                    end
                    loop Precheck every supplied scopes[j] in input order before parent/child mutation
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check duplicate permission scope
                        infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Check duplicate permission scope
                        activate t_permission_scope
                            note right of t_permission_scope
                                SELECT
                                    ps.id as permission_scope_id
                                FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                                WHERE ps.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                                AND ps.scope_id = '<sequence.permissions.scopes.scopeId>'
                                AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                AND ('<sequence.permissions.scopes.id>' IS NULL OR ps.id <> '<sequence.permissions.scopes.id>') -- omitted child insert id is typed SQL NULL
                            end note
                            t_permission_scope -> infra: Return non-DELETED same scope pair excluding optional child id in pre-write state
                        deactivate t_permission_scope
                        infra -> app: Return non-DELETED same scope pair excluding optional child id in pre-write state
                        alt Another non-DELETED definition has this scope pair
                            break Reject entire batch
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 permissions[i]: Scope already exists in the permission.
                                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                        alt Child rowStatus = DELETED
                            app -> infra: QUERY - Check role permission scope in use
                            infra -> t_role_permission_scope: QUERY - Check role permission scope in use
                            activate t_role_permission_scope
                                note right of t_role_permission_scope
                                    SELECT
                                        rps.id as role_permission_scope_id
                                    FROM author.t_role_permission_scope rps
                                    WHERE rps.permission_scope_id = '<sequence.permissions.scopes.id>' -- only when the scope item is deleted
                                    AND rps.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                end note
                                t_role_permission_scope -> infra: Return non-DELETED role-scope references to this definition
                            deactivate t_role_permission_scope
                            infra -> app: Return non-DELETED role-scope references to this definition
                            app -> infra: QUERY - Check user permission scope in use
                            infra -> t_user_permission: QUERY - Check user permission scope in use
                            activate t_user_permission
                                note right of t_user_permission
                                    SELECT
                                        up.id as user_permission_id
                                    FROM author.t_user_permission up
                                    WHERE up.permission_scope_id = '<sequence.permissions.scopes.id>' -- only when the scope item is deleted
                                    AND up.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                end note
                                t_user_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED direct-user references to this definition
                            deactivate t_user_permission
                            infra -> app: Return non-DELETED direct-user references to this definition
                            alt Either non-DELETED child reference exists
                                break Reject entire batch
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 409 E10006 permissions[i]: Scope is used by roles or users.
                                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                                end break
                            else Check passed
                            end
                        else Child rowStatus = ACTIVE
                        end
                    end
                    alt Parent id omitted (INSERT, including ARCHIVED)
                        app -> infra: INSERT - Create permission
                        infra -> m_permission: INSERT - Create permission
                        activate m_permission
                            note right of m_permission
                                INSERT INTO author.m_permission (
                                    created_by,
                                    created_at,
                                    row_status,
                                    name,
                                    description
                                )
                                VALUES (
                                    &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.now>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.permissions.rowStatus>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.permissions.name>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.permissions.description>'
                                )
                                RETURNING id as permission_id
                            end note
                            m_permission -> infra: Return inserted permission_id
                        deactivate m_permission
                        infra -> app: Return inserted permission_id
                        app -> app: Require exactly one inserted parent UUID; missing/malformed result is internal failure
                    else Parent id supplied (UPDATE, DELETE or ARCHIVE)
                        app -> infra: UPDATE - Update or delete permission
                        infra -> m_permission: UPDATE - Update or delete permission
                        activate m_permission
                            note right of m_permission
                                UPDATE author.m_permission
                                SET
                                    updated_by = '<sequence.updatedBy>',
                                    updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                    row_status = '<sequence.permissions.rowStatus>',
                                    name = '<sequence.permissions.name>',
                                    description = '<sequence.permissions.description>'
                                WHERE id = '<sequence.permissions.id>'
                                AND row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                RETURNING id as permission_id
                            end note
                            m_permission -> infra: Return guarded returned permission_id or no row
                        deactivate m_permission
                        infra -> app: Return guarded returned permission_id or no row
                        alt Parent UPDATE returned zero rows
                            break Reject entire batch
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 permissions[i]: Permission not found.
                                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                        app -> app: Require exactly one returned parent id equal to request id; mismatch is internal failure
                    end
                    app -> app: permissionId = actual parent RETURNING id; bind this server-derived id for all child writes and final queries
                    loop Apply every supplied scopes[j] in input order atomically
                        alt Child id omitted
                            app -> infra: INSERT - Create permission scope
                            infra -> t_permission_scope: INSERT - Create permission scope
                            activate t_permission_scope
                                note right of t_permission_scope
                                    INSERT INTO author.t_permission_scope (
                                        created_by,
                                        created_at,
                                        row_status,
                                        permission_id,
                                        scope_id
                                    )
                                    VALUES (
                                        &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                        &#39;<sequence.now>',
                                        &#39;<sequence.permissions.scopes.rowStatus>',
                                        &#39;<sequence.permissionId>',
                                        &#39;<sequence.permissions.scopes.scopeId>'
                                    )
                                    RETURNING id as permission_scope_id
                                end note
                                t_permission_scope -> infra: Return inserted permission_scope_id
                            deactivate t_permission_scope
                            infra -> app: Return inserted permission_scope_id
                            app -> app: Require exactly one inserted child UUID; missing/malformed result is internal failure
                        else Child id supplied
                            app -> infra: UPDATE - Update or delete permission scope
                            infra -> t_permission_scope: UPDATE - Update or delete permission scope
                            activate t_permission_scope
                                note right of t_permission_scope
                                    UPDATE author.t_permission_scope
                                    SET
                                        updated_by = '<sequence.updatedBy>',
                                        updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                        row_status = '<sequence.permissions.scopes.rowStatus>'
                                    WHERE id = '<sequence.permissions.scopes.id>'
                                    AND permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                                    AND scope_id = '<sequence.permissions.scopes.scopeId>'
                                    AND row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                    RETURNING id as permission_scope_id
                                end note
                                t_permission_scope -> infra: Return guarded returned permission_scope_id or no row
                            deactivate t_permission_scope
                            infra -> app: Return guarded returned permission_scope_id or no row
                            alt Child UPDATE returned zero rows
                                break Reject entire batch
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 permissions[i]: Permission scope not found.
                                    api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                    page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                                end break
                            else Check passed
                            end
                            app -> app: Require exactly one returned child id equal to input id; mismatch is internal failure
                        end
                    end
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Count permission scope definitions
                    infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Count permission scope definitions
                    activate t_permission_scope
                        note right of t_permission_scope
                            SELECT
                                COUNT(ps.id) as definition_count
                            FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                            WHERE ps.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                            AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        end note
                        t_permission_scope -> infra: Return definitionCount including every non-DELETED definition
                    deactivate t_permission_scope
                    infra -> app: Return definitionCount including every non-DELETED definition
                    app -> app: finalDefinitionCount = definitionCount; require valid nonnegative integer
                    alt Current permission rowStatus = DELETED and finalDefinitionCount > 0 (Q24)
                        break Reject the entire batch
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 409 E10006 permissions[i]: Permission cannot be deleted while scope definitions remain.
                            api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Q24 passed
                        app -> app: Q24 passed for permissions[i]: rowStatus is not DELETED or finalDefinitionCount = 0
                    end
                    alt beforeDefinitionCount > 0 and finalDefinitionCount = 0 (Q22 transition)
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check role permission in use
                        infra -> t_role_permission: QUERY - Check role permission in use
                        activate t_role_permission
                            note right of t_role_permission
                                SELECT
                                    rp.id as role_permission_id
                                FROM author.t_role_permission rp
                                WHERE rp.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>' -- destructive parent check or final Q22 guard
                                AND rp.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            end note
                            t_role_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED role grants for this permission
                        deactivate t_role_permission
                        infra -> app: Return non-DELETED role grants for this permission
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check user permission in use
                        infra -> t_user_permission: QUERY - Check user permission in use
                        activate t_user_permission
                            note right of t_user_permission
                                SELECT
                                    up.id as user_permission_id
                                FROM author.t_user_permission up
                                WHERE up.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>' -- destructive parent check or final Q22 guard
                                AND up.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            end note
                            t_user_permission -> infra: Return non-DELETED direct-user grants for this permission
                        deactivate t_user_permission
                        infra -> app: Return non-DELETED direct-user grants for this permission
                        alt Either fresh non-DELETED role/direct-user grant survives
                            break Reject entire batch
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10006 permissions[i]: Permission cannot become unscoped while assigned to roles or users.
                                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                    else Permission remains scoped or was already unscoped
                        app -> app: Q22 does not prohibit existing unscoped grants
                    end
                    app -> app: Map exactly index=i, permissionId=actual parent RETURNING id, action=INSERT when id omitted else DELETE/ARCHIVE/UPDATE from requested status; include every delete result
                    app -> app: Append this one result in original input order; no child ids or rowStatus in response
                end
                app -> app: Require result count = input count, indices 0..n-1 in order, unique returned parent UUIDs and exactly index/permissionId/action per item; data = exactly permissions; finish all mapping
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return all committed permission and scope-link actions
                note over app, infra
                    Q22/Q23 approved by the product owner on 2026-11-08. The detailed revision remains in-review; no
                    backend/schema implementation.
                    Every permission follows the rules of [the single upsert](../04-upsert-permission/spec.md#permission-rules):
                    name is the permission code: lower-case letters, DELETED is final, delete and archive are rejected while a
                    role (`author.t_role_permission`) or a user (`author.t_user_permission`) that is not DELETED still holds it.
                    An item without `id` is added, with `id` is updated, with `rowStatus` DELETED is removed. Scopes that are
                    not listed are kept. Adding/retaining an ACTIVE link requires an ACTIVE master (404 E10005); deleting an
                    existing owned link skips that master-status test under owner Q23. A scope cannot be deleted from the
                    permission while a role (`author.t_role_permission_scope`) or a user (`author.t_user_permission`) still uses
                    it (409, E10006). A permission without scopes has no scope dimension.
                    Authorize once after all target existence checks and before scope/conflict work; valid non-admin claims
                    return one 403 E10009 with no item index. Approved by the product owner (Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13); no live
                    caller-assignment fallback.
                    Reject duplicate parsed canonical parent ids, and exact duplicate names among non-DELETED input permissions,
                    with 400 before SQL. Deleted input items do not reserve names. Every supplied scopes is an array (null
                    invalid); scopes omitted or [] means no link change. Each scope object allows only id/scopeId/rowStatus:
                    supplied id is a non-null UUID, required scopeId is a non-null UUID, status defaults to ACTIVE only when
                    omitted and permits ACTIVE/DELETED. Reject insert-DELETED, duplicate canonical child ids within one
                    permission and duplicate scopeIds among its non-DELETED input links. Required fields remain required for
                    deletes. No new scope-array limit is introduced. Item input errors use permissions[i]; envelope/count/header
                    errors have no invented index.
                    activeScopeIds contains only scopeIds requested ACTIVE anywhere in the batch; permissionScopeIds contains
                    all supplied child ids. Lock ACTIVE masters globally, then requested non-DELETED definitions restricted to
                    targetPermissionIds, both sorted by id. Map each returned child id to its stored permission_id and scope_id.
                    For a current permission bind permissionId to its verified target id or typed SQL NULL for an insert;
                    optional permissions.id, callerUserId and derived permissionId are distinct. After parent RETURNING replace
                    permissionId with the actual returned UUID for child writes and final reads.
                    Q23 owner answer: “ใช่ อนุญาตถอน link ของ scope ที่ปิดแล้ว”. Removing an existing owned link permits an
                    INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED/DELETED master; ownership, immutable scopeId, non-DELETED reference and Q22 checks
                    still apply. ACTIVE link creation/retention still requires an ACTIVE master. No master or grant row is
                    changed.
                    Capture beforeDefinitionCount as every non-DELETED definition of the current permission, irrespective of
                    definition/master status. Run name/child duplicate and parent/link in-use checks before this permission's
                    parent/child writes. Name uniqueness spans all non-DELETED parents; optional parent/child insert ids bind
                    typed SQL NULL with null-safe exclusions. Every child precheck precedes the current parent's first write:
                    deleting then readding the same existing scopeId within its array still conflicts in pre-write state.
                    Omitted/unlisted links are kept.
                    After all of the current permission's parent/child writes, query finalDefinitionCount again. Q22 triggers
                    only when beforeDefinitionCount > 0 and finalDefinitionCount = 0, then freshly query non-DELETED
                    role/direct-user grants. Any surviving grant gives 409 E10006 permissions[i]: Permission cannot become
                    unscoped while assigned to roles or users. and rolls back every item, link and audit change. Owner answer:
                    “ใช่ ปฏิเสธจนถอน grant เดิมครบ”. Already-unscoped metadata updates may keep valid unscoped grants. Because
                    parent ids cannot repeat and child ownership is enforced, this post-item state is that permission's final
                    whole-request state; no later item may alter its definitions. Count all non-DELETED definitions, not only
                    ACTIVE or ACTIVE-master ones.
                    Q24 approved by the product owner on 2026-11-09: owner answered “ต้องถอน links ให้ครบก่อนลบ permission
                    (แนะนำ)”. After the current permission's child writes, reuse finalDefinitionCount before Q22 or result
                    mapping. If rowStatus = DELETED and finalDefinitionCount > 0, return 409 E10006 `permissions[i]: Permission
                    cannot be deleted while scope definitions remain.` and roll back the entire batch, including earlier
                    permissions, links and audit writes; return no partial results. Count every non-DELETED definition
                    (ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED), even if its master is closed. Omitted scopes, [] and partial withdrawal
                    do not bypass this check. Complete explicit withdrawal and parent deletion in one request are allowed
                    subject to ownership, immutable-id and reference checks. A parent with only DELETED history may be deleted.
                    No implicit cascade; ARCHIVED and other reversible parent states may retain definitions. The
                    no-duplicate-parent and child-ownership rules make this per-item post-write count the permission's final
                    whole-request state. This prevents new stranded definitions without approving a legacy-data rewrite or a
                    deleted-parent cleanup endpoint.
                    Parent/child INSERTs explicitly set server created_at and must return exactly one UUID; missing/malformed
                    results are generic 500. Parent UPDATE guards id/non-DELETED; child UPDATE guards id/derived
                    permissionId/immutable scopeId/non-DELETED. A zero-row update is indexed 404 E10004; returned existing ids
                    must match input ids. Preserve creation audit. Parent archive and reversible states keep unlisted child
                    definitions. Parent delete requires no non-DELETED definitions after explicit child actions (Q24); keeping
                    an unlisted live definition rejects the entire batch. Explicit child actions remain atomic and there is no
                    implicit cascade. No grant history is rewritten.
                    Append exactly index/permissionId/action from RETURNING for each permission, original zero-based index and
                    order; action is INSERT for omitted id (including insert-ARCHIVED), otherwise DELETE for DELETED, ARCHIVE
                    for ARCHIVED, UPDATE for ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED. Include delete results. Require one result per input, no
                    duplicate returned parent ids and exactly data.permissions. Complete Q24 and Q22 for every permission.
                    Finish all mapping before one COMMIT after the outer loop; then one HTTP 200 S10000 Batch Upsert Permission
                    Success. No item-level 201/204, rowStatus, child ids or partial result is returned.
                    Every item-specific 400/404/409 has permissions[i] prefix; authorization 403 has no item position. SQLSTATE
                    23505 from uq_m_permission_name maps to indexed 409 E10003 Permission name already exists.;
                    uq_t_permission_scope_permission_id_scope_id maps to indexed 409 E10003 Scope already exists in the
                    permission. Both roll back all earlier items. Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failures are request-level
                    generic 500 without bizCode; timeout before COMMIT is request-level 408 E90001 after rollback. No retry is
                    promised for an unknown commit result.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Batch Upsert Permission Success; exactly data.permissions
                api -> page: Show the complete ordered batch result including deletes
                page -> user: Display all committed permission actions
            else SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_m_permission_name at current writing item
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 permissions[i]: Permission name already exists.
                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
            else SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_t_permission_scope_permission_id_scope_id at current writing item
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 permissions[i]: Scope already exists in the permission.
                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Reject the entire batch; no results or partial success
                page -> user: Display failure; keep all unsaved input
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
